## Layer Structure

Create root containers once in `src/scene/layers/layers.js` and add everything to a layer, never directly to the stage. This gives you predictable z-ordering without sorting.

```js
// scene/layers/layers.js
import { Container } from 'pixi.js';
import { app } from '@/utils/app';

export const backgroundLayer = new Container();
export const worldLayer = new Container();
export const uiLayer = new Container();
export const overlayLayer = new Container();

export function setupLayers() {
  app.stage.addChild(backgroundLayer, worldLayer, uiLayer, overlayLayer);
}
```

- Add order = draw order. Later children render on top.
- Only set `sortableChildren = true` on containers that genuinely need dynamic depth sorting — it costs a sort every frame.
- For cross-hierarchy ordering, use **RenderLayers** rather than reparenting.

