## Ticker Loop

The ticker loop lives entirely in `main.js`. Pixi's ticker gives you `deltaTime` (frame-normalized) and `deltaMS` — convert to seconds for all physics and gameplay.

```js
// main.js
import { app, initApp } from '@/utils/app';
import { setupLayers } from '@/scene/layers/layers';
import { loadAssets } from '@/utils/assets';
import { setupScene } from '@/scene/setup';
import { updateEnemies } from '@/systems/updateEnemies';

async function main() {
  await initApp();
  setupLayers();
  await loadAssets();
  await setupScene();

  app.ticker.add((ticker) => {
    const deltaSec = ticker.deltaMS / 1000;

    updateEnemies(deltaSec);
  });
}

main();
```

- Pass `deltaSec` (seconds) to all update functions — never raw `deltaTime`
- Each system gets its own `update*(deltaSec)` function in its own file under `systems/`
- `main.js` only orchestrates — no business logic
- To cap framerate: `app.ticker.maxFPS = 60`

