## Responsive Resizing

Design against a fixed logical resolution, then scale the root container to fit. This keeps gameplay coordinates stable across devices.

```js
// utils/resize.js
import { app } from '@/utils/app';
import { config } from '@/config/config';

const { designWidth, designHeight, fitMode } = config.layout;

export function setupResize(rootContainer) {
  const handleResize = () => {
    const scaleX = window.innerWidth / designWidth;
    const scaleY = window.innerHeight / designHeight;
    const scale = fitMode === 'cover' ? Math.max(scaleX, scaleY) : Math.min(scaleX, scaleY);

    rootContainer.scale.set(scale);
    rootContainer.position.set(
      (window.innerWidth - designWidth * scale) / 2,
      (window.innerHeight - designHeight * scale) / 2
    );
  };

  handleResize();
  window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);
}
```

For playable ads and portrait/landscape switching, keep two layout config blocks and swap positions on orientation change rather than relying on scale alone.

