## Performance Checklist

- Cap resolution: `Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2)`
- Use spritesheets so sprites batch into single draw calls
- Keep sprites using the same texture adjacent in the display list — texture swaps break batching
- Set `eventMode = 'none'` on non-interactive containers
- Avoid `sortableChildren` unless dynamic depth sorting is genuinely required
- Pool everything spawned repeatedly
- Use `BitmapText` for frequently-updating text
- Use `container.cacheAsTexture()` for complex static subtrees — remember to disable it if contents change
- Call `.destroy({ children: true, texture: false })` when tearing down a scene; keep shared textures alive
- Avoid filters on large containers — each filter is a full render pass
- Set `renderer.background.alpha = 0` rather than drawing a full-screen Graphics rect

---

## Avoid

- Hardcoding numbers in scene files — put them in `config.js`
- v7 API: `new Application({...})` without `await app.init()`, `app.view`, `PIXI.Loader`, `beginFill()/endFill()`, `interactive = true`
- Adding display objects directly to `app.stage` — use a layer container
- Loading textures inside entity files — load through the `Assets` manifest
- Creating a new `TextStyle` per `Text` instance
- Global side effects on import — export functions, not immediate execution
- Forgetting `pointerupoutside` — drags will stick when the pointer leaves the target
- Destroying and recreating objects per-frame instead of pooling
